  "lessons": "- **Indigenous and Canadian community news:** Consistently favored: First Nations advocacy, reconciliation, land stewardship, and substantive civic or community stories (housing, hospice planning, local fire bans, arts funding, 4-H and agriculture pipelines). Sports recaps, routine event listings, and empty portal pages are rejected.\n- **Environmental framing:** Accepted when the angle is solutions, protection, policy stakes, Indigenous rights, or industry pivots with clear stakes (water, microplastics, persistent chemicals, impact assessments). Pure disaster or weather coverage (wildfire evacuations, smoke, heat) is mostly rejected, though occasional high-impact disaster reporting has landed.\n- **EV and automotive:** Accepted for automaker strategy, corporate turnarounds, charging infrastructure milestones, and battery breakthroughs. Rejected for ownership decline, sales drops, model reveals, spec-sheet reviews, luxury car showpieces, and car listicles.\n- **Science & nature discovery:** Strongly favored: surprising natural phenomena, animal and evolutionary biology, cross-species behavior, astronomy, geoscience, critical minerals, and novel research with real-world implications. Wellness pseudoscience, longevity checklists, and symptom-driven health advice are rejected; neurologically or environmentally grounded health research can land.\n- **AI & tech policy and risk:** Accepted for security vulnerabilities, attacks or manipulation of AI systems, disclosed hacks, legal rulings, expert warnings about societal impact, and critiques of bubbles or overreach. Product launches, model hype, feature updates, funding deals, executive moves, and assistant-app coverage are rejected.\n- **Practical tech and consum",
